{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_5a5f5cce8b0c4534b78a45f54533e7e9","id":"pg_98f7f231e4415467ad1ffb12693a4e00","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/esengine-deepseek-reasonix-docs-acp-zh-cn-md-8679e1f0b614-fb12693a4e00.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_bbe7024d85b65ec889e80d27031201c9"],"title":"esengine/DeepSeek-Reasonix/docs/ACP.zh-CN.md @ 8679e1f0b614","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5a5f5cce8b0c4534b78a45f54533e7e9"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_21363203e0d16a36e77c20e30ff62c28629db51f56eb9331d3e79c5f67dcc4fe"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Reasonix implements Agent Client Protocol v1 as an NDJSON JSON-RPC 2.0 agent over stdin/stdout, launched via `reasonix acp`, with diagnostics sent to stderr."},{"claim_ids":["clm_30aba16090a5c19f0648f37a29def9e3550668490d5b538de0f1c2ff6eceeebb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ACP exposes session lifecycle methods including session/new, load, resume, prompt, cancel, list, close, and delete, each session owning an isolated controller, workspace root, model, and transcript."},{"claim_ids":["clm_44183ae25a0abfc887cd7e2b66eebd2e869c60d133b5a891384bd60e3b845b15"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Permission presets are read-only, workspace-write, and danger-full-access; tool-approval changes update the gate in place without rebuilding the session controller."},{"claim_ids":["clm_914cecc3c84bfac1020fca791a18c6320ef4fae15a9104da1016f89375c9057a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A durable session inbox extension supports enqueue, list, get, update, delete, move, setPaused, retry, and refresh operations on persisted follow-up work."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a7426a9beb75edf6263e23d284cbb6a84a1c91ed6488ce8ff01da51d48897d62"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"When the ACP client advertises fs.readTextFile, fs.writeTextFile, or terminal capabilities, eligible file operations route through editor unsaved buffers and foreground commands through a client-owned terminal; non-UTF-8 files stay on the local path."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b3568155dda85e633753e0ea9b6c02fdc0302fbd51a590cd9a9e40269d7d4be1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A vendor extension `_reasonix.io/session/steer` provides mid-turn guidance, returning steer_accepted or queued_followup after durably committing the guidance."},{"claim_ids":["clm_da8966472920f310d6957f187da3ab5271b2f032c0595a1bd6d17c7cfceae7c6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Session controls are split into independent axes: collaboration mode (normal/plan/goal), model, reasoning effort, and permission preset (read-only, workspace-write, danger-full-access), set via session/set_config_option."}],"claim_ids":["clm_21363203e0d16a36e77c20e30ff62c28629db51f56eb9331d3e79c5f67dcc4fe","clm_30aba16090a5c19f0648f37a29def9e3550668490d5b538de0f1c2ff6eceeebb","clm_44183ae25a0abfc887cd7e2b66eebd2e869c60d133b5a891384bd60e3b845b15","clm_914cecc3c84bfac1020fca791a18c6320ef4fae15a9104da1016f89375c9057a","clm_a7426a9beb75edf6263e23d284cbb6a84a1c91ed6488ce8ff01da51d48897d62","clm_b3568155dda85e633753e0ea9b6c02fdc0302fbd51a590cd9a9e40269d7d4be1","clm_da8966472920f310d6957f187da3ab5271b2f032c0595a1bd6d17c7cfceae7c6"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_5a5f5cce8b0c4534b78a45f54533e7e9","id":"pg_b6241eeceeae577680fef595215f6040","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/esengine-deepseek-reasonix-docs-acp-md-8679e1f0b614-f595215f6040.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_294a47589e8a579e94ec3d5329cac65d"],"title":"esengine/DeepSeek-Reasonix/docs/ACP.md @ 8679e1f0b614","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5a5f5cce8b0c4534b78a45f54533e7e9"}
